      <!-- =====================================================
           02 / ON THE BENCH
           ===================================================== -->

      <section class="section work" id="work">

        <div
          class="section-heading"
          data-reveal
        >
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">02 / ON THE BENCH</p>

            <h2>
              WE'RE TESTING THE PROCESS ON REAL SHAPES.
            </h2>
          </div>

          <div class="section-intro">
            <p>
              We're developing fabrication methods by putting them against
              increasingly difficult sign work.
            </p>

            <p class="section-intro-emphasis">
              Channel letters are one place we're starting.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>


        <div class="work-grid">

          <article
            class="work-card featured"
            data-reveal
            style="--reveal-delay: 0s"
          >
            <div>
              <div class="card-top">
                <span class="card-index">01</span>
                <span class="card-type">CURRENT TEST CASE</span>
              </div>

              <h3>Tight Geometry</h3>

              <p>
                Small channel-letter components are one of our first proving
                grounds: tight curves, narrow returns, interior features,
                fit, finishing, and dimensional accuracy all show up quickly.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card-status">
              <span class="status-dot"></span>
              ACTIVE PROTOTYPING
            </div>
          </article>


          <article
            class="work-card"
            data-reveal
            style="--reveal-delay: .10s"
          >
            <div>
              <div class="card-top">
                <span class="card-index">02</span>
                <span class="card-type">CAPABILITY TEST</span>
              </div>

              <h3>Unusual Geometry</h3>

              <p>
                Curves. Intersections. Tight details. Shapes that make the
                manufacturing method part of the problem.
              </p>

              <p>
                We want to find out where a different approach holds up—and
                where it doesn't.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card-status secondary">
              UNDER EVALUATION
            </div>
          </article>


          <article
            class="work-card"
            data-reveal
            style="--reveal-delay: .20s"
          >
            <div>
              <div class="card-top">
                <span class="card-index">03</span>
                <span class="card-type">OPEN TERRITORY</span>
              </div>

              <h3>One-Offs & Short Runs</h3>

              <p>
                Some parts aren't repeated enough to justify designing an
                entire production process around them.
              </p>

              <p>
                We're interested in what becomes practical when the method
                can change with the job.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card-status secondary">
              SHOW US WHAT YOU'VE GOT
            </div>
          </article>

        </div>

      </section>


      <!-- =====================================================
           QUOTE
           ===================================================== -->

      <section class="pullquote">

        <div data-reveal>

          <p class="eyebrow">
            OUR POSITION
          </p>

